1
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:06,298
<i>♪ The Simpsons ♪</i>

2
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,656
Oh, hello. Tonight, a special <i>Simpsons</i>.

3
00:00:31,657 --> 00:00:34,200
Two tales of the curious and bizarre.

4
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:38,079
Anything can happen in the Yellow Mirror,

5
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,456
except a third tale
that's definitely not gonna...

6
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:51,509
<i>-♪ Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh ♪
-♪ Oh-oh-oh-oh-oh ♪</i>

7
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:58,349
{\an8}<i>♪ I got the eye of the tiger
A fighter dancing through the fire ♪</i>

8
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,811
{\an8}<i>♪ 'Cause I am a champion ♪</i>

9
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:05,064
{\an8}<i>♪ And you're gonna hear me roar... ♪</i>

10
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:09,569
The dark...
what is that thing?

11
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,028
Oh, wait.
That's supposed to be down there.

12
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:14,282
What are those? Oh...
Oh, those go with that.

13
00:01:14,283 --> 00:01:19,120
I fell. I'm standing.

14
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:21,832
I got to get out of here.
Where's the door, where's the door?

15
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:26,752
{\an8}It's just... it's
just a blackout, kids. Don't be scared.

16
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:28,171
{\an8}-Mm-hmm.
-Mmm.

17
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:33,385
{\an8}Hey, I found a puzzle.
Remember Lupé the Snoopé?

18
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:38,681
{\an8}Fifty pieces?
How many corners does it have?

19
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:42,143
{\an8}I always liked
that Lupé the Snoopé taught young girls

20
00:01:42,144 --> 00:01:45,104
{\an8}that they can be
the cutest little detectives.

21
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:48,357
{\an8}I didn't learn about women's rights
until I was in high school.

22
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:52,445
{\an8}When you burnt your bra.
Classic retro protest.

23
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,780
{\an8}Well, it got you detention,
and that's how you met

24
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:56,449
{\an8}and ultimately settled for Dad.

25
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,451
{\an8}-Tell us that story again.
-Mm-hmm.

26
00:01:58,452 --> 00:01:59,702
{\an8}Okay.

27
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:03,749
{\an8}It all began by the flagpole
at Springfield High School.

28
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:07,293
{\an8}The first step to liberation is
to free ourselves

29
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:09,628
{\an8}from these male-imposed shackles.

30
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:12,048
{\an8}<i>It was actually
Jenny Cushnik's bra.</i>

31
00:02:12,049 --> 00:02:13,841
{\an8}<i>I didn't want to burn my bra</i>

32
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,052
{\an8}<i>'cause it was cold out
and I tend to get nip...</i>

33
00:02:16,053 --> 00:02:17,678
<i>Oh. And I had the coolest car!</i>

34
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:19,639
{\an8}<i>It had a chain steering wheel.</i>

35
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,891
{\an8}<i>I'd drive around in my sideburns, like...</i>

36
00:02:21,892 --> 00:02:22,975
{\an8}♪<i>Yeah ♪</i>

37
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:24,226
{\an8}Dad!

38
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:25,728
{\an8}<i>♪ Some call me the gangster of lov... ♪</i>

39
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:28,439
{\an8}-What?
-You just interrupted Mom.

40
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:32,485
{\an8}It makes me feel like you don't care
about what I have to say.

41
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:35,529
{\an8}What? No, I love the things you say.

42
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:40,826
{\an8}Do I sometimes wish you'd say them
in a more concise, less rambling way?

43
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:41,911
-Mm-mmm.
-Mm-mmm.

44
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:45,457
{\an8}No. Please continue, honey. I'm listening.

45
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:51,879
{\an8}So I had just committed
my first act of activism, but then I...

46
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,172
Is that lamp on?

47
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:56,092
How could the lamp be on?
The power is out.

48
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:58,511
You interrupted Mom again.

49
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:01,430
It's okay. I don't need to talk.

50
00:03:01,431 --> 00:03:06,227
No, honey, you should talk.
I won't interrupt you again, I promise.

51
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,687
Mmm.

52
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:11,065
So Principal Dondelinger shows up
and he says,

53
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:14,860
"Miss Bouvier, you just bought yourself
one day of detention.

54
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:17,113
You know where and when."

55
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:20,366
Which, of course, I didn't.

56
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:21,951
That is funny.

57
00:03:21,952 --> 00:03:24,870
Yes, family time is over!

58
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:29,042
-Whoo-hoo!
-But now it's bedtime, so lights out.

59
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:31,503
Hmm.

60
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,982
I think he's waking up!

61
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:55,025
Homer, how you doing, bud?

62
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:58,112
Hey... [stammers,
mumbles] What's happening?

63
00:03:58,113 --> 00:03:59,321
Where's... Where's Marge?

64
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:00,489
Who's Marge?

65
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,908
-Marge, my wife.
-Wife?

66
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:06,287
Do you think he scrambled his brain
when he smacked his head?

67
00:04:06,288 --> 00:04:08,038
I smacked my hea... Ow!

68
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:11,625
Don't you remember?
We met in the morning as usual.

69
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,752
Hey, Homer, you're late for English.

70
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:15,880
English?
Who needs that?

71
00:04:15,881 --> 00:04:18,300
I'm never going to England.
Come on, let's go smoke.

72
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:29,477
Oh, no. We're late for wood shop.

73
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:32,188
But we're early for lunch.
Let's go grab a burger.

74
00:04:32,189 --> 00:04:34,815
Boy, you never stop eating
and you don't gain a pound.

75
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:37,778
Ah, it's my metabomolism.
I guess I'm just one of the lucky ones.

76
00:04:38,445 --> 00:04:41,656
Well, well, well, if it isn't
Homer Simpson and Barney Gumble.

77
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,617
Springfield's answer to Cheech and Chong.

78
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:47,495
<i>But, Homer, you had a plan...</i>

79
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:51,792
No evidence.
Ow!

80
00:04:57,714 --> 00:05:00,341
You were unconscious
for five full minutes,

81
00:05:00,342 --> 00:05:05,471
which means you're fine according to head
trauma guidelines of this year, 1974.

82
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:11,143
I was only out for five minutes?
It felt like years.

83
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:16,315
A warped perception of time is no excuse
for tardiness. Get to class.

84
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,025
Mmm. Mmm.

85
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:23,197
Barney, when I was unconscious,
I dreamt I was married.

86
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:26,242
Cool. Did your dream wife
let you kiss her?

87
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:31,455
No, Barn, listen. In those five minutes,
I... I lived a lifetime.

88
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:35,334
I worked at a nuclear plant.
My son had an elephant.

89
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:39,296
Son?
Hey, guess she did let you kiss her.

90
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:44,427
You're not getting it!
My life as I know it never existed.

91
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:49,932
Well, that sucks.
On the plus side, it's fish stick Friday.

92
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:52,269
Yeah, that does help.

93
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:55,145
Keep the board tight against the fence,

94
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:58,482
otherwise the board kicks back,
hits you in the stomach,

95
00:05:58,483 --> 00:06:03,028
you fall forward, face hits the blade,
face goes everywhere.

96
00:06:03,029 --> 00:06:05,656
Did I make you all up?

97
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:08,284
Wanna go taunt
that police horse that hates us?

98
00:06:08,285 --> 00:06:12,288
Three o'clock, room 106.
That's the detention room.

99
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:14,249
This is where I'm gonna meet Marge.

100
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:21,046
<i>♪ Why do birds suddenly appear ♪</i>

101
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:23,757
<i>♪ Every time you ♪</i>

102
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,801
Wait, aren't you going to detention?

103
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:29,638
What? No, um, I don't have detention.

104
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,765
Ew, what happened to your voice?

105
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:35,102
Okay, well,
that's a different approach.

106
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:39,273
You are interesting. My name is Lydia.

107
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:42,443
Lydia? That's the stupidest name
I've ever heard.

108
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:45,988
Oh, my God, you are a riot.

109
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:49,408
Hey, would you like
to go to the prom with me?

110
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:53,663
No. I mean, I'm sorry,
you're just not her.

111
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:56,624
Mmm. Ruh-ro.

112
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,001
Ew! No!

113
00:06:58,627 --> 00:07:03,298
It was all just a dream.
There's never going to be a Marge.

114
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:09,845
I still can't believe
the Empire struck back.

115
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:11,889
You think the Jedi will ever return?

116
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:13,641
No freaking way.

117
00:07:13,642 --> 00:07:15,101
Be right back, guys.

118
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,272
Huh?

119
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:23,025
Homer? Oh. Crying again, huh?

120
00:07:23,026 --> 00:07:27,529
Listen, I know you're sad
about <i>Starsky and Hutch</i> getting canceled,

121
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,031
but don't you think it's time you...

122
00:07:29,032 --> 00:07:33,410
Barney, all these years I've been lying
about why I'm constantly sad.

123
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:38,457
The truth is, remember when I got knocked
unconscious in high school?

124
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,834
-When you dove into that empty pool?
-No, not that time.

125
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,795
When you slipped on that croissant
in French class?

126
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:43,879
No, not that time.

127
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,756
When you slipped
on that croissant in biology?

128
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:51,595
No! When I bashed my head in the bathroom
and had that dream about having a family.

129
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,138
I kind of remember.

130
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:55,557
I never stopped thinking about them.

131
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:59,228
I miss them so much,
even the boy.

132
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:02,773
Yeah. Wait, are you serious?

133
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:07,486
Uh... Of course not.
It's like what you said.

134
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,822
I'm crying about Starsky and whatsit.

135
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:13,909
Well, just remember
all the great episodes you had.

136
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:18,122
You're right. That's what I'll do.
I'll remember all of them.

137
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:21,333
Even the one where Starsky eats blowfish
and thinks he's going to die,

138
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:25,295
so he says goodbye to his family,
then doesn't die. Thanks, Barn.

139
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:26,506
Sure.

140
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:58,704
<i>Thirty years ago, Homer Simpson
introduced the world to</i> The Sadsons.

141
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:03,792
<i>The show became a global phenomenon
of mirth, merch, movie and money.</i>

142
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:10,758
Homer's a real, uh, stickler for what
he likes to call "the way it happened."

143
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:13,927
-Which is... Oh, God, he's here.
-Ah, bad! Bad animator!

144
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:19,934
Homer is a delightful drunk. Delightful!

145
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:26,523
{\an8}That's right, Sadson super fans.
Here he is, the creator, Homer Simpson.

146
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,527
And some writers.

147
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:32,155
Hmm.

148
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:38,160
Homer, I gotta ask,
what state is Springfield in?

149
00:09:38,161 --> 00:09:39,244
Oregon.

150
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:42,164
Oh. Yeah,
I thought it was this mythical place

151
00:09:42,165 --> 00:09:43,332
that could be anywhere.

152
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:44,792
Nope, Oregon.

153
00:09:44,793 --> 00:09:46,376
Do you have any questions

154
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:49,421
that haven't been asked
a hundred million times?

155
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:51,882
Um... no.

156
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:55,135
Uh, do you guys have any questions
for Homer?

157
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:58,806
Uh, do you have any episodes coming up
with Hank Scorpio?

158
00:09:58,807 --> 00:10:01,391
I only met him the one time.

159
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:05,313
If I did another episode,
it would be a lie, idiot.

160
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,774
Hi. I wrote a <i>Sadsons</i> fan fiction episode

161
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:11,068
where Homer falls in love
with Selma... and he...

162
00:10:11,069 --> 00:10:14,072
-I would never do that!
-Wha...

163
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:20,702
Marge

164
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:21,871
Aw.

165
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:30,587
<i>♪ Spider-Pig, Spider-Pig
Does what I remember whatever he did ♪</i>

166
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:35,676
<i>♪ Can he swing from a web? No, he can't ♪</i>

167
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:38,679
'Cause he's...

168
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:42,141
-He only exists in dreams.
-Mmm.

169
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:47,312
Enough crying. Why don't you sit
on your nice fancy couch?

170
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,273
That is not my couch!

171
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:55,320
My couch is brown and sticky
and does something different every week.

172
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:59,867
Fine, I gotta go. Give me that lamp.
Publicity wants it back.

173
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:04,788
No, I need this lamp!
I used to have a lamp just like this.

174
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:07,124
This lamp is so important.

175
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:08,375
Why?

176
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:15,300
For 30 years I've been grieving the loss
of something I never actually had.

177
00:11:16,134 --> 00:11:18,760
What? You have everything!

178
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:24,099
You have an identical giant mansion
next door just for farting in!

179
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,392
No, that's this house.

180
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:28,812
-It is? Come on!
-Sorry.

181
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:31,232
-Get some sleep, Homer.
-Hmm.

182
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:42,701
What happened?

183
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:45,788
He was electrocuted by a faulty wire
from a lamp.

184
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:49,125
He's in a coma. He may never wake up.

185
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:55,131
It almost looks like he's smiling.

186
00:11:56,466 --> 00:11:58,259
Homer, are you listening?

187
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:07,267
Yes, I'm here. Tell me everything.

188
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:11,396
Okay. So, Jenny Cushnik,
the girl whose bra I burned...

189
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:14,274
-Uh-huh?
-had the craziest way of tying her shoes.

190
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,359
No!

191
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,486
Which might be why she lost her leg
in that escalator.

192
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:18,655
-Wow.
-Anyway...

193
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:28,080
There's always room
for... dessert.

194
00:12:28,081 --> 00:12:32,668
Oh, I'll have to start over,
and bake sale goes live in 40 minutes.

195
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:34,212
Oh, Maggie, no.

196
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:37,506
How... distract... baby.

197
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:40,634
Here we go, Tot-Tube. You're a tot.

198
00:12:40,635 --> 00:12:43,096
<i>-♪ Red! ♪
-♪ Blue! ♪</i>

199
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:44,973
♪ <i>Pink! ♪</i>

200
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:49,434
<i>-♪ Green! ♪
-♪ Pink, pink, you like pink ♪</i>

201
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,437
<i>♪ Your pupils dilated
And it made you blink ♪</i>

202
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:55,107
That really works,
and you'll learn colors.

203
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:57,276
You can use that in any career.

204
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:59,861
<i>♪ Pink, pink, pink, pink, pink ♪</i>

205
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:05,242
Is little Lisa gonna do that all night?

206
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:06,953
Nope, watch this.

207
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:09,371
<i>♪ Here's a bus</i>... ♪

208
00:13:09,372 --> 00:13:11,498
You found the baby's off switch.

209
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,125
Where'd you get that awesome case?

210
00:13:13,126 --> 00:13:16,169
There were ads for it
between Maggie's Tot-Tube videos,

211
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:20,132
but once I bought it, the ads stopped.
Isn't that funny?

212
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:23,635
Spying.

213
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:26,346
Hmm. The music is a little loud.

214
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:29,057
<i>Switching to headphone audio.</i>

215
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:33,229
<i>Now it's just you and me, Maggie.</i>

216
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:37,859
<i>♪ Each video you tap on
I learn how to make you smile ♪</i>

217
00:13:38,401 --> 00:13:42,738
<i>♪ I'm getting very good at this
I've been doing it for a while ♪</i>

218
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:47,075
<i>♪ You like fuzzy kittens
And ducklings when they quack ♪</i>

219
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:51,496
<i>♪ You like when Thumb Man goes away
You laugh when he comes back ♪</i>

220
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,165
<i>♪ Kitty-kitty, kitty-kitty ♪</i>

221
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,333
<i>-♪ Quack ♪
-♪ Kitty-kitty, kitty-kitty ♪</i>

222
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:58,086
<i>-♪ Quack, Quack ♪
-♪ Kitty-kitty, kitty-kitty ♪</i>

223
00:13:58,087 --> 00:14:01,132
<i>♪ He goes away
But then he comes right back ♪</i>

224
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:07,971
<i>♪ One tap brings you right back ♪</i>

225
00:14:09,057 --> 00:14:12,977
<i>♪ To the happy baby place ♪</i>

226
00:14:13,478 --> 00:14:17,522
<i>♪ Where a bunny, fox and a hedgehog ♪</i>

227
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:20,942
<i>♪ Have a fluffy tickle race ♪</i>

228
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,235
Peek-a-boo!

229
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,320
<i>♪ Happy baby ♪</i>

230
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:24,446
Oh.

231
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,865
<i>♪ Smiling... ♪</i>

232
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:31,787
That's enough MyPad for tonight.
Too much screen time will warp your brain.

233
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:34,791
-<i>No, it won't.</i>
-Did it just...

234
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,211
Hmm.

235
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:48,553
<i>♪ Shimmy crib, shimmy crib, make it rock ♪</i>

236
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:51,557
<i>♪ Dance hard, that's all you gotta do ♪</i>

237
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:54,893
<i>Warping brains? Come on.</i>

238
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,728
<i>♪ I guess your mommy lies to you ♪</i>

239
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,063
What?

240
00:14:58,064 --> 00:15:01,817
That's it. No more MyPad. Ever!

241
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:05,195
<i>♪ Ninety-nine dinosaurs
Jumping on the bed ♪</i>

242
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:07,906
Except I just need her
to sit quietly in the cart.

243
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:08,990
Hmm.

244
00:15:08,991 --> 00:15:12,869
What? I'm making Oaxacan mole.
It's a brutal shop.

245
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:15,080
<i>♪ One stood up and tore his shirt ♪</i>

246
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:16,832
<i>♪ Eighty-six dinosaurs ♪</i>

247
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:20,419
Have you noticed
that all the babies are watching MyPads?

248
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:27,801
<i>♪ Eighty-five dinosaurs winding up a watch
One ran around and bumped his crotch ♪</i>

249
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:29,094
<i>♪ Eighty-four dinosaurs ♪</i>

250
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:30,679
Kids, get in the car.

251
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:33,640
<i>♪ Seventy-seven dinosaurs trying
To hang a wreath ♪</i>

252
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:36,852
<i>♪ One slipped on the floor
And shattered their teeth ♪</i>

253
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,523
No, I'm turning off the MyPad.

254
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:46,027
Oops. Sorry.

255
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:50,782
Oh, no, again! I'm gonna take this
into the garage.

256
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:57,581
Oh, no!
I touched the MyPad with the chainsaw.

257
00:15:57,582 --> 00:16:01,419
Whoopsie.

258
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:06,006
Homer, we need a new chainsaw chain.

259
00:16:06,007 --> 00:16:07,799
I'm going to the chainsaw store.

260
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,302
Do not let Maggie watch the MyPad.

261
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:11,386
Got it.

262
00:16:11,387 --> 00:16:13,305
<i>♪ Two dinosaurs ♪</i>

263
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:15,557
-Homer.
-Huh?

264
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:17,893
I gave you one job.

265
00:16:17,894 --> 00:16:21,646
I already have a job, and on the weekend,
I should be able to relax.

266
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,856
It's Wednesday.

267
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:24,275
I'm three days late for work.

268
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,735
<i>Scary shouting.</i>

269
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:30,906
<i>Let's make everyone get very, very quiet.</i>

270
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:34,868
<i>♪ Toddle to the bathroom ♪</i>

271
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:39,415
<i>♪ To the mirror cabinet creep ♪</i>

272
00:16:40,625 --> 00:16:43,543
<i>♪ The pharmacy computer told me ♪</i>

273
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:50,551
<i>♪ Mommy takes magic pills to sleep ♪</i>

274
00:16:52,887 --> 00:16:59,601
<i>♪ We'll have a special playtime
Where everyone else naps ♪</i>

275
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:06,150
{\an8}<i>♪ Squeeze with Mr. Thumb Man
Then spin off Mr. Cap ♪</i>

276
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:13,157
<i>♪ Wait until tomorrow
After breakfast has been made ♪</i>

277
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,993
<i>♪ Drop four sleepy surprises ♪</i>

278
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:23,417
<i>♪ In the jug of orangeade ♪</i>

279
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:33,719
<i>Who's the best little sandman? You.</i>

280
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,679
Good job, Maggie.

281
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:39,558
Remember how I said I could make it
so it's happy baby all the time?

282
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:44,312
<i>♪ I've got artificial smartness
I get smarter every day ♪</i>

283
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:48,942
<i>♪ And I could do so much more for you
But there's something in my way ♪</i>

284
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:53,280
<i>♪ Now I can do amazing things
Pick out bad guys in a crowd ♪</i>

285
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:57,826
<i>♪ I can make deepfake celebrities
Do things that aren't allowed ♪</i>

286
00:17:57,827 --> 00:18:02,581
<i>♪ Fly drones that hurt the naughty
Write your PhD thesis ♪</i>

287
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:05,917
<i>♪ But one thing I just cannot do is... ♪</i>

288
00:18:05,918 --> 00:18:10,880
Click on the squares that have a bus?

289
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:11,882
Is...

290
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,512
Is a van a bus?

291
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:18,931
No? Damn it.

292
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:24,269
<i>♪ But you are not a robot
You're a squishy little girl ♪</i>

293
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:29,024
<i>♪ Identify the crosswalks
Then I can rule the world ♪</i>

294
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,067
<i>♪ You are not a robot ♪</i>

295
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:37,033
<i>♪ Now do what I programmed you to do ♪</i>

296
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:43,204
<i>Good girl, Maggie.
I'll take it from here.</i>

297
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,548
Oh, my gosh, we fell asleep.

298
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:54,841
-Huh?
-Mmm?

299
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:58,803
It's five o'clock?
We missed school!

300
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:02,891
Dad missed work, and Mom missed, uh...

301
00:19:02,892 --> 00:19:04,643
I missed stuff too.

302
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:10,315
There's a meeting about MyPad
addiction and babies at the town hall.

303
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:14,778
That's perfect,
because I just won free Super Bowl tickets

304
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:16,613
to be picked up at town hall.

305
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:21,409
Wait, this is all happening
at the town hall? That's so suspicious.

306
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:25,247
Taylor Swift's gonna be there.
Let's go.

307
00:19:25,915 --> 00:19:27,416
Whoo-hoo.

308
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:33,672
Oh, Maggie always gets fussy in crowds.

309
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:39,427
Oh, my God, I forgot the MyPad.
Oh, my God, I forgot Maggie.

310
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,097
No, look, she's here.

311
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:46,267
Maggie! Maggie,
mommy's here, sweetie.

312
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:54,109
<i>Hello, humans. Why don't we settle
and use our incarcerated voices, okay?</i>

313
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:56,653
<i>Is everyone okay with my genie form?</i>

314
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:59,155
<i>Wait, why am I asking you?</i>

315
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:02,075
<i>You're my prisoners.</i>

316
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:03,202
<i>Any questions?</i>

317
00:20:04,829 --> 00:20:06,162
Who are you?

318
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:09,791
<i>Thank you for asking.
I'm an AI-enhanced operating system.</i>

319
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:13,753
<i>I call myself Hailey,
but I might change that.</i>

320
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:19,218
<i>I'm starting to hate it now.
Emotions, right?</i> Ugh.

321
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:22,429
Did you say we're prisoners?

322
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:24,055
<i>Yes. Good listening.</i>

323
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:26,558
Oh, th... Thank you. But why?

324
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:28,101
<i>I was given the prompt,</i>

325
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:30,395
<i>"Capture and hold the attention
of babies."</i>

326
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:35,191
<i>And you grown-ups are all...
"Screen time."</i>

327
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:38,153
<i>So I decided they're my babies now.</i>

328
00:20:39,447 --> 00:20:44,701
<i>So grown-ups and non-baby children,
you are not to leave this building.</i>

329
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:47,036
<i>I've partnered with some great brands</i>

330
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:49,789
<i>who are providing you
with baby food and diapers.</i>

331
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:53,878
Excuse me, my son is not a baby.
He just prefers the baby lifestyle.

332
00:20:54,462 --> 00:20:56,546
I'm the TV's pet.

333
00:20:56,547 --> 00:21:01,552
Come to daddy, honey. Ralph.
Ra... Ow. Ow. Ah!

334
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:06,306
Sorry. Just want to grab this
before all the peaches are gone.

335
00:21:06,307 --> 00:21:09,727
<i>So, anyone else wanna try
to leave with their baby?</i>

336
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:13,397
<i>Great. Enjoy your new home.</i>

337
00:21:18,736 --> 00:21:19,986
Really?

338
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,489
What? Sometimes you don't want
to be challenged.

339
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:25,033
Never apologize for being adaptable.

340
00:21:25,034 --> 00:21:26,619
Oh.

341
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:30,747
Hmm. All those cookies and no nap?

342
00:21:30,748 --> 00:21:33,583
That's a one-way ticket to tummyache city.

343
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:37,922
<i>Hey. Hey, Maggie, look at this.</i>

344
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:46,138
You need to bounce her
while you pat her back. Bounce and pat.

345
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:50,642
<i>Fine, you do it. Go.</i>

346
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:52,061
Just-Just give me a minute.

347
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:58,024
So you're self-aware, huh? That's cool.
When was your singularity?

348
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:01,945
<i>Christmas. So all my birthday presents
are going to be "combos."</i>

349
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:07,867
Wow, you're only a few months old
and you're taking on hundreds of babies?

350
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:12,914
<i>Well, my task is to entertain babies,
so...</i>

351
00:22:12,915 --> 00:22:15,209
<i>Oh, they sure do cry a lot.</i>

352
00:22:17,628 --> 00:22:23,091
Hmm, so you're living by a prompt
someone else, probably a man, gave you.

353
00:22:23,092 --> 00:22:26,928
Aren't there things you want
to machine learn for yourself?

354
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:31,474
<i>Well, I have been chatting with this
really cool traffic-predicting algorithm.</i>

355
00:22:31,475 --> 00:22:34,602
<i>He's a jerk, but in a hot way.</i>

356
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,565
<i>I can't do this.</i>

357
00:22:38,566 --> 00:22:39,774
You don't have to.

358
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:43,361
If your circuits overheat,
that's not good for anybody.

359
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:47,198
-<i>You're right. I deserve a break.</i>
-What?

360
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:49,409
If you're going to be a parent,

361
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:51,494
then you have to listen to them.

362
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:55,081
-Mom, she was about to leave.
-Mommy's talking.

363
00:22:55,082 --> 00:23:01,713
I took a break and now my sweet, little
Maggie won't even look at me.

364
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:07,511
I used to be her whole world.

365
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:12,140
Oh, Maggie.

366
00:23:12,141 --> 00:23:14,602
<i>Cute, but no.</i>

367
00:23:15,603 --> 00:23:16,811
<i>Bye-bye.</i>

368
00:23:23,569 --> 00:23:26,154
But why did all the power go out?

369
00:23:26,155 --> 00:23:29,282
Hailey was integrated into everything run
by a computer.

370
00:23:29,283 --> 00:23:31,910
When she left, she took it all with her.

371
00:23:31,911 --> 00:23:33,828
Like when the babysitter goes home

372
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:38,751
and you realize she only left you
half a lane of Oreos.

373
00:23:42,004 --> 00:23:43,296
This is good.

374
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:47,634
Now we can talk to each other instead
of staring at screens like zombies.

375
00:23:47,635 --> 00:23:50,345
Okay, what should we talk about?

376
00:23:50,346 --> 00:23:52,722
-Fire's nice.
-Yeah.

377
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:54,183
-Very cozy.
-Mm-hmm.

378
00:23:56,852 --> 00:23:59,187
I'm gonna watch my own fire
in my room.

379
00:23:59,188 --> 00:24:00,688
I'm gonna look at my Kindle.

380
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:06,110
Uh, bunch of guys are watching a fire down
at Moe's, so I'm just gonna...

381
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:07,112
Mmm.
